      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "\"Hot\" worlds seem to be ordered based on the \"heat\" property of maps on the vrchat site/api, which seems to be based on what maps are currently popular in a short time frame. I've noticed this resets every month.\n\"Classics\" looks like its just the popular tab renamed.\n\nI think the \"Hot\" category is a decent addition as a lot of the \"Classics\" maps that rank highly are older maps and its harder for new maps, even those that have gotten popular to gain visibility there hence the addition of the \"Hot\" category.  Having it reset is good for refreshing the list and giving new maps equal opportunity for visibility. \n\nI'd like to see recently updated back as well as maps that are not as visible due to not being popular or visited often have little opportunity of letting people know they've been updated and there's reason to visit.\n\nA row I'd like to see is recommended maps, that recommends you maps you've never been to before based on your own map visit history and or favourites, by using some sort of recommendation system based on the visiting/favourite patterns of the vrchat community. Of course, this is probably quite difficult and a long term goal perhaps.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
