  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-06-19T13:20:43.525Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I recommend removing hot and putting the Active worlds at the top. I'm pretty sure these are technically the \"hot\" worlds since they sort by how many players they have. \n\nmaybe replace it with worlds being quickly favourite or something in a certain time like past 48 hours if you must have something like that.. \n\nAlso why is Active my platform and Active cross platform still separated on pc. If we can get to them both then they are on our platform no need for 2 columns. This is literally only sort of handy for quest users and even then not since they cannot get on none cross platform? Its unessarsary to have 2 rows when it could be taking up less space. \n\nAlso what is the purpose of Classic's? When a world is memorable surely the playerbase would suggest it to players or continue to be there Preferably this should be randomised from maps out of a certain time frame as this just comes across as something to keep older players happy from complaining.  At least move it out of second place as Spotlight should be second. \n\nIt makes no sense that the active rows are where they are.\n\nCommunity labs should be on top of new and should also be prioritised near the top. \n\nBasically I suggest - \n\nActive worlds (Combined on PC)\n\nSpotlight (So we know some new or updated maps that stand out)\n\nCommunity Labs (So we know whats new new)\n\nNew (So we know whats new out of community labs)\n\nRecently Updated (So we see whats been updated)\n\nRandom (Nice idea adding this btw)\n\nAvatar Worlds (Players like to get these before games)\n\nGames (Picked out avatar time to play)\n\nRecent\n\nMine\n\nFavourites\n\n-----------\n\nHopefully a NEW UI on the way.",
